# Heart events and friend-day scenes for Tilda, Juno and Piper (wave 2). Compiled to zz_fs_wave2_events.json.

dialogue tilda.slate
n0 tilda: This is the slate. Every small kindness in Wetherell, in chalk. Marcus is two planks ahead of Odalys. She doesn't know yet.
  next n1
n1 tilda: I ruled you a column the day you arrived. It's been waiting. What do I write under your name?
  ? A thank-you, in big letters. => r0 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.slate.thanks
  ? A joke. A good one. => r1 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.slate.joke
  ? A promise. I'll keep it. => r2 | friend:tilda,15 | flag:choice.slate.promise
r0 tilda: A thank-you. Hard to cash, and I'll never spend it. My favorite currency.
  expr happy
r1 tilda: A joke! On my slate! ...Oh, that's good. Don't tell anyone I laughed in the shop.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: A promise. I'll write it small. I'll hold it large.

dialogue tilda.hours
n0 tilda: I count the stock at closing time. Lately the count comes out right and the street comes out short.
  expr thinking
  next n1
n1 tilda: Wetherell isn't shrinking, I tell myself. Then a whole morning brings two customers, and I can name them both. What do you think?
  ? It isn't shrinking. I'm staying. => r0 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.hours.reassure
  ? Let's fill the shop together. => r1 | friend:tilda,15 | flag:choice.hours.plan
  ? Count again, then. Gently. => r2 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.hours.joke
r0 tilda: Staying. ...Say it once more, slower. I'd like it on the slate in your handwriting.
r1 tilda: Together. Now that's a plan I'd stock. Bring ideas. I'll bring the tea, and the good cups.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: Gently. Recounting with kindness. I'll try it. Ledger can check my sums.

dialogue tilda.card
n0 -: Behind the flour sacks, in a very old tin, lies a recipe card in faded ink.
  next n1
n1 tilda: My mother's pumpkin pie. The only thing she ever wrote down. I've never baked it. What if I get it wrong?
  ? Bake it. I'll stand right there. => r0 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.card.bake
  ? Keep it safe. It's enough. => r1 | friend:tilda,10 | flag:choice.card.keep
  ? Share it. The pie feud can cope. => r2 | friend:tilda,15 | flag:choice.card.share
r0 tilda: Bake it. Yes. With you by the oven, so I can't back out.
  expr happy
r1 tilda: Safe. It's been safe for forty years. That's not a bad record.
r2 tilda: The whole village. ...The pie feud will be livid. I love it.
  expr happy

dialogue juno.label
n0 juno: So? Say something. Any answer except 'Hm.' I get enough of that at work.
  ? Wear it proudly. => r0 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.label.accept
  ? Relabel her right back. => r1 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.label.relabel
  ? Eat the label. => r2 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.label.eat
r0 juno: Accepted! You're officially a fixture. I'll sweep around you and dust you on Fridays.
  expr happy
r1 juno: Relabel me? Brilliant. Here's the pencil. ...'Apprentice (Chaotic)'. Fair. Stick it right here.
  expr happy
r2 juno: You... ate it. You ate my label. ...I'm labeling this moment 'Do Not Repeat'. Please repeat it.
  emote sweat

dialogue juno.strike
n0 juno: My first piece that isn't a copy of anything. A little horseshoe. It's lopsided. I made it. I hate how much I love it.
  expr sad
  next n1
n1 juno: So. Keep it, or the barrel? Quick, before my arm decides.
  ? Keep it. It's yours. => r0 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.strike.keep
  ? Let's fix the bend together. => r1 | friend:juno,15 | flag:choice.strike.together
  ? Laugh about it with her. => r2 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.strike.laugh
r0 juno: Keep it. Yes. Even crooked. ...Especially crooked.
  expr happy
r1 juno: Together? You hold the tongs, like the first day. I tap the bend. Ready? Go!
  expr happy
r2 juno: It's very funny! A horseshoe for a three-legged horse. A very proud three-legged horse.
  expr happy

dialogue juno.shoe
n0 -: Bram stands at the far end of the forge. Juno holds the horseshoe out in both hands and keeps her eyes on the floor.
  next n1
n1 juno: I can't look. What's his face doing? Is it the 'Hm' face or the other 'Hm' face?
  ? Wait with her, quietly. => r0 | friend:juno,15 | flag:choice.shoe.wait
  ? Tell her it's wonderful. => r1 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.shoe.praise
  ? Hand her the hammer. => r2 | friend:juno,10 | flag:choice.shoe.hammer
r0 juno: ...Okay. Quiet's good. The anvil's being quiet too. Everyone is being so quiet.
r1 juno: Wonderful? It's crooked! ...But okay. I'm looking up now. Slowly. Very slowly.
  expr happy
r2 juno: The hammer? Okay. One more tap. For luck. For me. For crooked things everywhere.
  expr happy

dialogue piper.request
n0 piper: The room's waiting. A ballad, a jig, or my parsnip masterpiece? Choose wisely. Choose parsnips.
  ? A ballad, please. => r0 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.request.ballad
  ? A jig! Get them dancing. => r1 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.request.jig
  ? The parsnip song. Obviously. => r2 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.request.parsnip
r0 piper: A ballad. Sad in the middle, happy at the end. Like a good harvest. Gather round.
  emote note
r1 piper: A jig! Mind your boots. The good stool's been waiting all night to dance.
  expr happy
r2 piper: The parsnip song! You have taste. Questionable, magnificent taste.
  expr happy

dialogue piper.fright
n0 piper: A hundred people, no blinking, every Friday. Tonight they'll notice the trick. The playing's real. The rest is volume.
  expr sad
  next n1
n1 piper: So. What do I do with that?
  ? Talk it through with her. => r0 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.fright.talk
  ? Sit beside her, quietly. => r1 | friend:piper,15 | flag:choice.fright.sit
  ? Drum along on a bucket. => r2 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.fright.bucket
r0 piper: Talk. Okay. I'm scared of quiet. Of being a good player and a forgettable writer. There. It's on the barrel now.
r1 piper: ...You didn't fill it. I always fill it. That's the job, I thought. ...Quiet's not so loud with two.
  expr happy
r2 piper: A bucket? You're drumming on a bucket? ...Okay. Okay! In four. One, two, three...
  expr happy

dialogue piper.chorus
n0 piper: The verse is about someone arriving. The chorus is about where they end up. What is it?
  ? Home. => r0 | friend:piper,15 | flag:choice.chorus.home
  ? The road. => r1 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.chorus.road
  ? This room. => r2 | friend:piper,10 | flag:choice.chorus.room
r0 piper: Home. ...Oh. Three months I've been circling that word. It just walked in and sat down.
  expr happy
r1 piper: The road. Wide and honest, and it rhymes with 'showed'. Too neatly. I don't trust a clean rhyme.
r2 piper: This room! A song about the saloon. The good stool is going to be unbearable.
  expr happy
